  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Let $r=\u27e8-5,1,3\u27e9$ and $s=\u27e8n,-2,4\u27e9.$ Given that the projection of $r$ onto $s$ is the zero vector, find the value of $n.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since $r$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $s$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\nr\u22a5s\\,\u27f9\\,r\\cdot s=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & ={r}_{x}\\cdot {s}_{x}+{r}_{y}\\cdot {s}_{y}+{r}_{z}\\cdot {s}_{z} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot n+1\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5n-2+12 \\\\  & =10-5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =0 \\\\ 10-5n & =0 \\\\ n & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
